<title>LATVIA: LATVIA - NEW CAR SALES RISE TO 1,697 BY JUNE 5.</title>
<headline>LATVIA - NEW CAR SALES RISE TO 1,697 BY JUNE 5.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of new cars rose to 1,697 units by June 5 from 1,239 at the end of April, the Latvian Motor Trader Association said on Monday.</p>
<p>The group said in a statement that the most popular car make so far this year is the Russian VAZ with 205 sales registered versus 176 in the year to end April.</p>
<p>The second most popular make was Renault with sales of 153 units versus 109 at the end of April and Toyota was third most popular vehicle make with sales of 142 units versus 109.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
